    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1579">

                <pb facs="1003" n="887" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg887"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.62/52.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            German Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I enclose, for your
                    information, a paraphrase of a telegram dated April 15, 1 p.m. from the American
                    Consul at Chihuahua, regarding the procedure in the matter of making
                    representations to the Constitutionalists in the case of the German subject
                    Radke.</p>
                <p>In this connection, I beg to invite your attention to a note the Department is
                    to-day addressing you on the subject of representations to General Venustiano
                    Carranza in behalf of the nationals of all foreign governments.<anchor n="152"
                        xml:id="d1579-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
